    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d174-a3">

                <pb facs="0339" n="253" sameAs="frus:frus1945Malta/pg253"/>

                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Enclosure 3]</seg>
                </opener>
                <p rendition="#center">
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Property of H. M. the King and Regency Council</hi>
                </p>
                <p>1. H. M. King Peter II can dispose of his estates and property in the country
                    during his absence. The superintendence of the Royal Estates will for that
                    period be under the supervision of the Regency Council.</p>
                <pb facs="0340" n="254" xml:id="pg254"/>
                <p>2. Regular intercourse between H. M. the King and the Regency Council will be
                    established and guaranteed.</p>
                <p>3. In case of disability, ill-health, death or resignation of one of the Regents,
                    H. M. the King will, on the proposal of the Government, appoint one other Regent
                    in his place.</p>
                <closer>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-left">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Belgrade</hi></placeName>, <date
                            ana="#date_imprecise-inferred-from-document-content"
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-12-07">December 1944</date>.</dateline>
                    <lb/><signed> J. B. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Tito</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dr. Ivan Subasic </hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>(Note by Embassy: The Croatian copy of the above agreement is dated December
                        7, 1944)</p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
